<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="025" project="teams-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Principal-agnostic collaboration endpoints (Option A) — dual-scheme /api/v1/external for CIAM + workforce (R2 FR-22)</title>
    <phase>2 BFF Workforce→Principal Resolver &amp; Membership (generalization)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth-critical change to SHARED collaboration endpoints; CIAM-regression risk (FR-15); the accessible-record-set enforcement is the core authorization boundary. code-review + adr-check mandatory.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security/auth-sensitive generalization of shared endpoints across two auth planes; high blast radius (CIAM regression) + becomes R2 platform foundation.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Serial BFF auth spine; shared ExternalAccess endpoints + AuthorizationModule.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>020,021,022,030,051,065</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, endpoints</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Generalize the collaboration BFF endpoints to be PRINCIPAL-AGNOSTIC (R2 FR-22): dual-scheme the existing /api/v1/external/* read + download endpoints to accept BOTH the CIAM scheme AND the workforce default scheme, resolve a plane-agnostic caller via a reusable CallerPrincipalResolver (CIAM contact by oid | workforce systemuser/contact via task 020's WorkforcePrincipalResolver), compose the common accessible-record-set (task 022) and apply the module's Tier-2 record predicate. Preserve the CIAM path EXACTLY (FR-15). This unblocks the Teams live E2E (task 080) AND is R2 Phase-P1 delivered early (per projects/teams-app-r1/notes/teams-app-r1-coordination.md — R2's decision was "proceed with Option A; it is foundational, not throwaway; do NOT build the parallel /collab data set (Option B)").
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform + authorization engineer. Expert in ASP.NET Core minimal-API multi-scheme auth (Microsoft.Identity.Web workforce scheme + a second CIAM JwtBearer scheme), the Spaarke external-access model (ExternalCallerContext, sprk_externalrecordaccess), the teams-app-r1 workforce plane (WorkforcePrincipalResolver 020, AccessibleRecordSetService 022, ContactStandingGrantReader 051), and two-tier authorization (module entitlement vs record scope). Follow ADRs + the R2 coordination guardrails strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    The /api/v1/external/* collaboration READ + DOWNLOAD endpoints (/me, /projects, /projects/{id}/documents, /projects/{id}/events|todos|contacts|organizations, document download) serve BOTH a CIAM external contact AND a workforce user (systemuser or contact) through ONE endpoint set, via a reusable CallerPrincipalResolver abstraction — never inline if(ciam)…else… . Each handler resolves caller → common accessible-record-set → applies the record predicate, so a workforce user sees ONLY their entitled records (NOT all projects). The CIAM path is byte-for-byte unchanged (regression-tested). /api/v1/collab is folded in or marked transitional. The live Teams tab loads records end-to-end. A coordination note is returned to R2 with the 8 required items.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Integration finding (2026-08-05): the Teams host authenticates via workforce NAA end-to-end, but the SPA's data layer (src/client/external-spa/src/api/web-api-client.ts) targets /api/v1/external/* which is CIAM-scheme-only (RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.CiamExternal), ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs ~L50-52). Task 020 built the workforce plane as a SEPARATE /api/v1/collab group with only /me (WorkforcePrincipalContextEndpoint) + broker download (task 030) — not the full data surface — so the workforce host 401s on every data call. R2 (spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2, FR-22 principal-agnostic endpoints + NFR-08 two-tier authz) decided Option A is the canonical pattern and this work is R2-P1 done early; Option B (parallel /collab data set + host-aware client) is rejected as throwaway.

      PHASE-0 VERIFIED (no config blocker): the BFF workforce default scheme IS the 1e40baad app — deployed AzureAd__Audience = api://1e40baad-e065-4aea-a8d4-4b7ab273458c, AzureAd__ClientId = 1e40baad-… (SDAP-BFF-SPE-API). The Teams NAA token (aud api://1e40baad-…, v1) validates against the workforce scheme with NO config change. AuthorizationModule.cs registers: workforce = JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme via AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApi(AzureAd); CIAM = AuthSchemes.Ciam via AddJwtBearer. AuthPolicies.CiamExternal pins /api/v1/external to the Ciam scheme.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalUserContextEndpoint.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/WorkforceCollaborationDownloadEndpoint.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalCallerContext.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/WorkforcePrincipalResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="output">projects/teams-app-r1/notes/r2-coordination-response.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <justification>
    <existing>Two parallel entry points today: /api/v1/external/* (CIAM, full data) + /api/v1/collab/* (workforce, only /me + download). WorkforcePrincipalResolver (020), AccessibleRecordSetService (022), ExternalCallerContext (CIAM) all exist.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — generalize the EXISTING /external endpoints + reuse AccessibleRecordSetService as the common set; the new CallerPrincipalResolver composes the two existing resolvers behind one abstraction. No new data endpoints, no new URL surface (R2 guardrail #4).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without this, the Teams workforce host authenticates but has zero data endpoints (401 on every /external call); the dual-host product cannot function, task 080 E2E cannot pass, and R2's FR-22 foundation is unbuilt.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="R2-guardrail-1">Build a single reusable CallerPrincipalResolver (ICallerPrincipalResolver + two strategies: CiamContactPrincipalStrategy resolving CIAM contact by oid/sprk_externalobjectid reusing ExternalCallerContext; WorkforcePrincipalStrategy wrapping task 020's WorkforcePrincipalResolver). Strategy is selected by WHICH SCHEME authenticated the request (inspect the authenticated identity's scheme/issuer), NOT by inline if(ciam)…else… in handlers. Handlers depend on the abstraction only. R2 lifts this component into the module framework as-is.</constraint>
    <constraint source="R2-guardrail-2">Handlers become principal-agnostic: resolve caller → { principal, accessibleRecordSet } (via AccessibleRecordSetService, task 022) → apply the module's Tier-2 record predicate to that set. No CIAM-contact assumptions baked into handler bodies.</constraint>
    <constraint source="R2-guardrail-3">Preserve the CIAM external path byte-for-byte in shape/behavior (R1 FR-15). Add a REGRESSION test asserting CIAM /me + /projects + /projects/{id}/documents + document-download responses are identical pre/post. NON-NEGOTIABLE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="R2-guardrail-4">Keep the /api/v1/external path — do NOT rename, fork, or invest in new URL surface. The resolver + dual-scheme logic carries forward if R2 later relocates the path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="R2-guardrail-5">Consolidate /api/v1/collab: fold its /me + download into the principal-agnostic /external surface (the SPA already calls /external/*), OR explicitly mark /collab transitional + slated for removal with a removal note. Do NOT leave two workforce entry points maintained indefinitely.</constraint>
    <constraint source="R2-guardrail-6 / ADR-028 NFR-02">Workforce path stays broker-only / no-OBO: the workforce token authenticates to the BFF only; downstream SPE/Dataverse stays app-only. MUST NOT exchange the workforce token downstream.</constraint>
    <constraint source="R2-guardrail-7">The workforce scheme audience acceptance is Phase-0-VERIFIED (AzureAd audience = api://1e40baad-…, matches the Teams token; v1 issuer handled by Microsoft.Identity.Web). Confirm this holds after the change and record it in the coordination note. No AzureAd audience config change is expected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="R2-NFR-08 (TWO-TIER — the priority item)">The workforce Tier-2 RECORD-SCOPE predicate MUST be a real, enforced predicate — a workforce user MUST NOT see all secure projects merely by authenticating. It is the accessible-record-set from AccessibleRecordSetService: systemuser → ADR-034 membership only; contact → sprk_externalrecordaccess grants ∪ standing-grant runtime membership (task 051). VERIFY the generalized /projects (and every read) handler filters by this set for a workforce caller, and DOCUMENT the exact predicate + code path in the coordination note. If any path today would grant a workforce user all projects, STOP and escalate — do not ship it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Publish size ≤60 MB compressed (baseline ~49.63 MB); report the delta; no M365 Agents SDK/Bot packages ADDED by this task (the pre-existing Microsoft.Agents.* from master are not this task's). Run /conflict-check before the BFF deploy.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Principal-agnostic dual-scheme collaboration endpoints (R2 FR-22)</topic>
