    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Multi-scheme policy" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs">Workforce (JwtBearerDefaults) + Ciam schemes already registered; a policy can set AuthenticationSchemes to accept BOTH so either token authenticates the /external group.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Common accessible-record-set" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs">Already composes per principal (systemuser membership; contact grants ∪ standing) — this is R2's common accessible-record-set; reuse it as the Tier-2 source for BOTH planes.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">PHASE 0 (already done, re-confirm): workforce scheme accepts api://1e40baad-… — verify no AzureAd audience change is needed.</step>
    <step order="2">PHASE 1 — CallerPrincipalResolver: define ICallerPrincipalResolver returning a plane-agnostic CallerPrincipal (kind, systemUserId?, contactId?, oid, tenantId, plane). Implement CiamContactPrincipalStrategy (reuse ExternalCallerContext CIAM resolution) + WorkforcePrincipalStrategy (wrap WorkforcePrincipalResolver). Select strategy by the authenticated scheme. Register in ExternalAccessModule DI.</step>
    <step order="3">PHASE 2 — Dual-scheme /api/v1/external: change the group auth to accept BOTH Ciam + workforce schemes (a policy with both AuthenticationSchemes, or per-endpoint). Refactor the read + download handlers to resolve caller via CallerPrincipalResolver → AccessibleRecordSetService → record predicate. Do NOT change the URL. Do NOT inline plane branching in handlers.</step>
    <step order="4">PHASE 3 — Workforce Tier-2 record-scope: verify each read handler filters by the accessible-record-set for a workforce caller (systemuser→membership; contact→grants∪standing). Confirm a workforce user does NOT get all projects. Capture the exact predicate + code path for the coordination note.</step>
    <step order="5">PHASE 4 — Consolidate /api/v1/collab: fold /me + download into /external (SPA calls /external/*), or mark /collab transitional with a removal note. No two workforce entry points.</step>
    <step order="6">PHASE 5 — Tests: (a) CIAM regression — /me + /projects + /documents + download identical pre/post (guardrail #3); (b) workforce — systemuser sees only membership projects, contact sees grants, non-member record → 403/omitted; (c) plane selection — Ciam token → CIAM strategy, workforce token → workforce strategy, no cross-selection.</step>
    <step order="7">PHASE 6 — dotnet build + dotnet test; publish-size report (≤60 MB); /conflict-check; deploy BFF to spaarke-bff-dev via scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1 (pwsh, hash-verify + health-check); smoke-test /api/v1/external/me unauthenticated = 401 (route registered).</step>
    <step order="8">PHASE 7 — write projects/teams-app-r1/notes/r2-coordination-response.md with the 8 items R2 requested (files touched; CallerPrincipalResolver shape + where a 3rd plane plugs in; workforce Tier-2 predicate + code path; CIAM regression evidence; v1 api://1e40baad audience confirmation; Entra recipe applied; /collab disposition; deviations).</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 025 ✅. Then the operator re-runs the live Teams E2E (task 080).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If dual-scheming /external cannot preserve the CIAM path byte-for-byte (a shared code path forces a CIAM behavior change), OR if the only way to make a read handler work for workforce is to grant all projects (violating NFR-08 Tier-2), STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 / §6.5 — do not ship a CIAM regression or an over-broad workforce scope.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test the BFF; publish-size; deploy via Deploy-BffApi.ps1</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands, /conflict-check, pwsh deploy</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/** (CIAM regression + workforce + plane-selection)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/teams-app-r1/notes/r2-coordination-response.md</output>
    <output type="deploy">Azure App Service spaarke-bff-dev (Sprk.Bff.Api)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A CallerPrincipalResolver abstraction exists with two strategies (CIAM contact, workforce), selected by the authenticated scheme; handlers depend on it, with NO inline if(ciam)…else… plane branching.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The /api/v1/external/* read + download endpoints authenticate BOTH a CIAM contact token AND a workforce token; the URL path is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A workforce systemuser sees ONLY their ADR-034 membership projects (NOT all projects); a workforce contact sees only grants ∪ standing-grant records; a non-member record returns 403/omitted — verified by test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The CIAM external path is byte-for-byte unchanged: a regression test asserts CIAM /me + /projects + /documents + download responses identical pre/post.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The workforce scheme validates the api://1e40baad-… (v1) audience with no AzureAd config change; confirmed + recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">/api/v1/collab is folded into /external OR explicitly marked transitional with a removal note (no two maintained workforce entry points).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF builds, tests pass, publish ≤60 MB, deployed to spaarke-bff-dev; the coordination note r2-coordination-response.md exists with all 8 R2 items.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-deploy, the live Teams tab loads the workspace + records for a workforce user (task 080 unblocked) — operator-verified in a live Teams client.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Net-new scope beyond the original minimal /collab plane — explicitly R2 Phase-P1 delivered early per the R2 coordination decision (notes/teams-app-r1-coordination.md). Do NOT build Option B (parallel /collab data set + host-aware client). The workforce Tier-2 record-scope predicate is the single most important thing to get right + document (R2 NFR-08). Entra config (multitenant, access_as_user, Teams client pre-auth 1fec8e78 + 5e3ce6c0, brk-multihub://green-dune-… SPA redirect, CSP framing) is ALREADY APPLIED to app 1e40baad on spaarkedev1/a221a95e — see notes/spa-v2-handoff-workforce-endpoint-gap.md §"Entra recipe". This task blocks task 080 (E2E) and the final wrap-up (090).
  </notes>

